{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017xtMUQ9DK7xFkPQAazPPbk","type":"tool_result","content":"30:even when no replayable snapshot can be recorded. The secret denylist is\n31-also owned here and consumed by the scope and context areas.\n32-\n33-Two `runs` subcommands operate on snapshots:\n34-\n35-- `npx roast runs checkout <run-id> [dir]` materializes a run's snapshot\n36-  into a detached linked worktree whose `git status`, `git diff HEAD`, and\n37-  `git diff --cached HEAD` reproduce the original state.\n38-- `npx roast runs prune` deletes aged refs under `refs/roast/snapshots/`.\n39-\n40-Run record layout and `meta.json` as a whole belong to the records area;\n41-this file specifies only the `snapshot` block and how it is filled.\n42-\n43-## Behavior contract\n44-\n45-### Constants\n46-\n47-- `REF_PREFIX = \"refs/roast/snapshots/\"`. Prune only ever deletes refs under\n48-  this prefix.\n49-- Default ref retention: 30 days (`720h`). Tighter than any artifact\n50-  retention because the refs live in the user's repository.\n51-- Snapshot commit identity (environment added to `commit-tree` only):\n52-  `GIT_AUTHOR_NAME=roast`, `GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL=roast@localhost`,\n53-  `GIT_COMMITTER_NAME=roast`, `GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL=roast@localhost`.\n54-  Capture must not fail on a machine with no `user.email` and must not\n55-  attribute Roast's object to the user. Dates are not overridden (an\n56-  inherited `GIT_COMMITTER_DATE` would apply).\n57-- Commit message: `roast run <run-id>`.\n58-- `file_modes` string recorded in `meta.json`, verbatim:\n59-  `regular and executable files plus symlinks; empty directories are not\n60-  represented` (one line, single space where wrapped here).\n61-- Temp directory prefixes (under `os.tmpdir()`): `roast-snapshot-`\n62-  (capture), `roast-pin-` (pin), `roast-checkout-` (checkout default\n63-  destination).\n64-\n65:### Secret denylist\n66-\n67-Default patterns, in this order:\n68-\n69-```\n70-.env*  *.pem  *_rsa  *.key  creds*\n71-id_rsa*  id_dsa*  id_ecdsa*  id_ed25519*  id_xmss*\n72-credentials.json  .npmrc  .pypirc  .netrc  _netrc  .pgpass\n73-.git-credentials  *.p12  *.pfx\n74-```\n75-\n76-`denylisted(path)`:\n77-\n78-1. Lower-case the path and every pattern (case-insensitive file systems\n79-   open `.ENV` as `.env`).\n80-2. A path matches if any pattern matches either its basename or the full\n81-   repo-relative path (`/`-separated), using Go `filepath.Match`\n82-   semantics: `*` matches any run of characters except `/` (a leading dot\n83-   is not special), `?` matches one character except `/`, `[...]` is a\n84-   character class (`^` negates, ranges `a-z`), `\\` escapes the next\n85-   character. A malformed pattern never matches (the error is swallowed).\n86-\n87-SSH keys are matched by key-type prefix so suffixed names\n88-(`id_ed25519_github`, `id_rsa_work`, `.pub` files) are covered; there is no\n89-bare `id_*` (it would drop `id_map.go`).\n90-\n91-`denylistedUntracked(repo, patterns?)` returns the untracked, non-ignored\n92-paths matching the denylist, sorted by byte order:\n93-\n94-- `patterns` omitted (Go `nil`) means the default list. An explicitly empty\n95-  list disables filtering and returns `[]` without running Git. No CLI path\n96-  passes a custom list; it exists for tests.\n97-- Runs `git -C <repo> ls-files --others --exclude-standard -z`, splits on\n98-  NUL, drops empty entries, keeps matches.\n99-- Tracked files are never denylisted here: their content is already in the\n100-  repository's history.\n101-\n102-### Git invocation rules\n103-\n104-Every Git call is `git -C <dir> <args...>` via `execFile`:\n105-\n106-- The child inherits the full process environment; per-call extra\n107-  variables are layered on top (so a per-call `GIT_INDEX_FILE` wins over an\n108-  inherited one). Calls without extras inherit `GIT_INDEX_FILE` unchanged,\n109-  except that restore calls clear it (see Restore, deliberate change 12).\n110-- The result is stdout with leading and trailing whitespace trimmed.\n111-- On a non-zero exit the error carries the exit status and, when present,\n112-  trimmed stderr (`<status>: <stderr>`); Git puts every useful message on\n113-  stderr.\n114-- Output can be large (`ls-files --others` on a big tree): the runner must\n115-  not truncate at Node's default `maxBuffer`.\n116-\n117-### Live index resolution\n118-\n119-The index a review reads, and therefore the one a snapshot copies:\n120-\n121-1. If `GIT_INDEX_FILE` is set in the process environment: that path; a\n122-   relative value is resolved against the repository toplevel (`repo`).\n123-   Under the native pre-commit gate Git points it at the temporary index\n124-   holding exactly the commit's content, which is what `--staged` reviews.\n125-2. Otherwise `<absolute-git-dir>/index`, where the Git dir comes from","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4913b683-6028-48ab-bf68-aa225d725bd4","uuid":"93548d20-6980-47dd-b79f-9b05dc8b94f6","timestamp":"2026-11-18T19:24:00.583Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"30:even when no replayable snapshot can be recorded. The secret denylist is\n31-also owned here and consumed by the scope and context areas.\n32-\n33-Two `runs` subcommands operate on snapshots:\n34-\n35-- `npx roast runs checkout <run-id> [dir]` materializes a run's snapshot\n36-  into a detached linked worktree whose `git status`, `git diff HEAD`, and\n37-  `git diff --cached HEAD` reproduce the original state.\n38-- `npx roast runs prune` deletes aged refs under `refs/roast/snapshots/`.\n39-\n40-Run record layout and `meta.json` as a whole belong to the records area;\n41-this file specifies only the `snapshot` block and how it is filled.\n42-\n43-## Behavior contract\n44-\n45-### Constants\n46-\n47-- `REF_PREFIX = \"refs/roast/snapshots/\"`. Prune only ever deletes refs under\n48-  this prefix.\n49-- Default ref retention: 30 days (`720h`). Tighter than any artifact\n50-  retention because the refs live in the