{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChAxp9JsbokB8sEDZQRDB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Ticket 10 is done: all 19 checklist items pass, everything is committed in 15 commits on this branch, and only `.redeye/notes.md` is left uncommitted, as instructed. Lint, typecheck, `npm run test:ts` (708 assertions) and the full `npm test` (Go tests plus launcher tests) all pass.\n\n**What was built**\n- **`src/scope/`:** `build`, `isEmpty`, `fit`, the types, the constants, `gitPatch` (streams git output into a `SectionCapper`), rename compaction, the linguist exclusions, the glob matcher, untracked-file synthesis and the byte-level helpers. `index.ts` is the public surface and re-exports the existing `gitRoot`.\n- **`src/snapshot/denylist.ts`:** the one shared copy of the secret denylist, built on the existing `goPathMatch`.\n- **Tests:** 12 new files under `test/scope/` plus `test/snapshot/denylist.ts`, all imported from `test/index.ts`. They run `build` against real temporary repos with their own `HOME`, XDG and global git config.\n\n**Where I departed from the spec, or you should know**\n1. **`diff.orderFile`:** git 2.49 rejects the empty value (`failed to read orderfile ''`), so `DIFF_CONFIG` uses the spec's fallback, `diff.orderFile=/dev/null`. The reversed-order test confirms it works: removing the override fails it for staged, committed and uncommitted builds.\n2. **`BuildOpts.env`:** this field isn't in the spec. The shared git runner takes the CLI's environment rather than reading `process.env`, so `build` needs a way to pass it through.\n3. **Huge-file memory test:** plain peak RSS growth was 14 to 37 MB whatever the file size. That comes from how Node frees discarded pipe chunks, not from buffering. The test forces a garbage collection while sampling and asserts:\n   - live memory (heap plus buffers) grows less than 3 MB (it measures about 1.2 MB);\n   - RSS grows less than the 24 MB file size.\n\n   Buffering git's output whole fails both checks. This measures live memory rather than the raw RSS the spec names. I also made the section capper skip dropped lines without creating a slice per line.\n4. **Non-UTF-8 names:** macOS's file system refuses them, so the on-disk test skips here. A second test puts such a name straight into the git index, so the skip-and-warn path is exercised on macOS too. Only names that would end up in `files` count toward the warning; counting the linguist listing would warn about unchanged files on every review.\n5. **Abort tests:** they show that git is killed and `build` rejects with an `AbortError`. They can't tell a swallowed abort apart from a rethrown one, because the next git call rejects on the aborted signal anyway. Every best-effort catch does rethrow on abort.\n6. **Repo scope:** `scope: \"repo\"` throws \"repo scope is not yet supported\" until ticket 25. `branch` and any other unknown value give the spec's error.\n\nI added the reusable conventions for this area (the `diffArgs` helper, the test-repo helper, the memory-measurement approach) to `AGENTS.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":181,"cache_read_input_tokens":232658,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":181},"output_tokens":769,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4913b683-6028-48ab-bf68-aa225d725bd4","uuid":"a6f3d8b1-c04c-4cfa-b254-bafe97375774","timestamp":"2026-11-18T19:41:46.655Z","request_id":"req_011ChAxp921YAuRnFv8EWEYW"}
